WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.435 --> 00:00:03.934
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:07.834
♪♪

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.968
Big news today,
as Pfizer announced that

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.033
a low dose of its vaccine
is safe and effective

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.501
for kids ages 5 to 11.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:18.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.067
It's great news until you hear
a 6-year-old say,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.534
"I want to do my own research
first."

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.267
Yeah, it's a version
of the Pfizer vaccine

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.033
that's much, much weaker,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.934
so they're calling it
Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:39.133
I think it's --
They -- They --

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.534
That's right. The vaccine
is highly effective

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:44.267
for kids 5 to 11, meanwhile
4-year-olds are like,

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.734
"Yeah, don't mind us, we'll just
keep Clorox-wiping our Legos.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.767
Okay?" Well...

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.901
Of course, a lot of kids
will get the vaccine,

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:55.534
while a small minority will
insist on taking pony dewormer.

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.300
Because they're children.
-Yeah, they're children.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.067
-Yeah, that's right.
-Not horse dewormer.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.701
-That's correct.
-Ponies are smaller.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.000
-Well, this is big news --
Pfizer decided to get

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.400
the word out with a new ad,
so...

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.534
I'm not sure they're sending
the right message, though.

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.067
Take a look at this.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.868
-We here at Pfizer are dedicated
to improving the lives

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.868
of our customers, whether it's
through our popular vaccine,

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.734
soon to be available
to children,

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.934
or through the thing the rest of
you know us for -- Viagra.

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.868
Pfizer -- we helped you make
your kids,

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.501
now let us keep them safe.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.501
-Interesting.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.934
[ Laughs ]

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.133
Very interesting.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:36.334
-Wow.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.100
-Meanwhile, out in California,
I saw that some McDonald's

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.534
locations are now offering
free vaccines.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:46.033
It's not every location,
so double check

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.834
before you let a clown
stab you with a needle.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.901
Just -- I'm just saying.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.901
Advice.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.467
Yeah, that's right.
It took 66 years,

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:57.901
but there's finally something
healthy at McDonald's.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.901
That's right, McDonald's
is offering vaccines.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.968
Man, those guys will do anything
to avoid fixing

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.334
the ice-cream machines.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.567
Anything. Just fix the thing!

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.634
Well, guys, this week,
world leaders are here

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:12.167
in New York City for the
United Nations General Assembly.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.701
Yeah, all the world leaders are
here, and if you think your job

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.467
is stressful, imagine telling
Brazil's unvaccinated president

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.567
he's not allowed in Sbarro's.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.300
Meanwhile in New York City,
Mayor Bill de Blasio

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.767
addressed world leaders
and said,

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.334
"If you don't want
to be vaccinated,

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.734
don't bother coming."

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.100
New Yorkers
agreed with the mayor.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.901
They were like, "Yeah, stay out!

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:38.634
And take de Blasio with you.
Take him, too."

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.467
[ Applause ]

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.501
Well, some more news here.
I saw that

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.901
former president Trump is trying
to find someone to replace

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.000
Mitch McConnell, even though
the GOP still supports him.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.400
So I guess now he's trying to
compromise by finding someone

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.300
who's similar to McConnell.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.100
Check out a few of the people
he's recommended.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:01.501
First up, there's Hans Moleman
from "The Simpsons."

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:04.634
Next up, there's a smiley face
french fry.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.834
After that, he recommended

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:12.100
SpongeBob SquarePants'
grandmother.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.367
And finally, he recommended
Harry Potter after using

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.567
the "old" filter on FaceApp.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:23.234
These are his recommendations.
-Wow.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.934
-I don't know.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.968
Hey, get this.
I heard that Beto O'Rourke

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:32.334
is preparing to run for
governor of Texas in 2022.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:33.968
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-They like this.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.534
Yeah, so Beto has run
for senator, president,

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.567
and now governor.
If he loses this race,

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:42.767
the only thing left is
condo-board treasurer.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.934
And finally,
two men in Australia

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.667
were arrested after they were
caught crossing the border

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:52.534
with $100,000
and a trunk full of KFC.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.133
Say what you want, but that cash

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.100
will never not smell like
fried chicken.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.501
♪♪

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.767
It's a very busy time
in New York City,

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:03.434
because the UN General Assembly
is officially under way.

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:06.100
Yeah. More than
100 foreign leaders are in town

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.167
to address the assembly,
while some are just here

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:11.100
to pick up a fiancée
for 90 days.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:14.968
I love when the UN General
Assembly is in session.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.634
There's no greater joy
than watching

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:19.367
the president of Romania
walk into the M&amp;M's Store.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.968
Seriously, when else
are you going to spot

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.567
the president of Latvia holding
one of those restaurant buzzers

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:27.834
outside Bubba Gump Shrimp?

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:31.234
It's like, "Our table is ready.
Let's go."

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:32.601
Of course, the main focus of

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.601
this year's General Assembly
is fighting COVID.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.968
Yep, nothing like holding
a superspreader event

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.601
to tackle a pandemic.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.801
There's actually some
real concern about

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.334
the General Assembly
turning into

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:48.033
a superspreader event,
because -- and this is real --

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:52.033
the UN is using the honor system
to check vaccinations.

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:54.701
-Ooh!
-What? The honor system?

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.234
I don't even trust
the honor system

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.767
when I give out candy
on Halloween.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:58.901
It's like, "Please take one.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.501
Oh, I know you're
going to take it.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.901
Honey, they took the bowl.
They --

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.767
We don't even have a bowl
anymore."

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.567
Next, the UN
is going to be like,

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:08.601
"We believe further conflict
with the Taliban

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:12.334
will be avoided thanks to
our latest pinkie promise."

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.801
The first leader
to speak this morning

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.000
and address the pandemic
was none other than

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.434
the unvaccinated president
of Brazil, Jair Bolsonaro.

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.501
Yeah, that's like attending
a weight-loss conference

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:27.734
and hearing, "Please welcome our
first speaker, Colonel Sanders."

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.934
After Bolsonaro spoke,
President Biden

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:34.667
then made his address
to the UN General Assembly.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.467
It was the first time he spoke
to a room of full of

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:37.734
world leaders
confidently knowing

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.968
that they didn't have him
on mute.

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:43.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:46.701
Yeah, Biden talked about
the pandemic, climate change,

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.400
and the withdrawal
from Afghanistan.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.567
When he watched, former
president Trump was like,

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:53.367
"Pssh!
I got way more laughs than him.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:56.367
Way more laughs."

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:57.734
People are talking about this.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.300
Today, the U.S. Space Force

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:02.534
unveiled a uniform prototype
for its members.

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:04.167
Finally. Look at this.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.567
Hmm.

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:09.133
Right now, every New York City
doorman is like,

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:12.467
"Are we in the Space Force?

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:14.033
What?

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:16.400
That's what we're wearing."

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.501
Can we see it again?

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.534
It looks like a line cook being
yelled at by Gordon Ramsay.

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:26.701
"Go to space with you, donkey!
Go to space!"

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.868
Seriously, by the time
you button up that jacket,

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:31.868
the space war is
going to be over, you know?

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:34.267
Yep, that is the new uniform,
until Jeff Bezos

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:36.334
buys the Space Force
and turns it into this.

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:40.467
Yeah, I love that.
He looks...

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:42.000
[ Applause ]

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.467
He looks like a mash-up
of Buzz Lightyear and Woody,

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:45.968
doesn't he?

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:47.467
Here's some good news.

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:50.400
Johnson &amp; Johnson announced
its COVID booster shot is

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.634
94% effective when given two
months after the first dose.

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.701
People who got the J&amp;J
were like,

00:06:56.701 --> 00:07:01.801
"Yeah, that would have been nice
to know about three months ago."

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.667
Actually, everyone
who got J&amp;J was like,

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:06.901
"We already got boosters.
They're called Moderna. Yeah."

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:09.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:10.734
Well, this is great.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:13.400
I saw that Google Meet --
Google Meet

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.567
is going to start automatically
adjusting webcam brightness

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.133
in users' browsers.

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:19.834
Yeah. And it's not the only
new feature they're adding.

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:21.167
Take a look at this.

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:22.934
-We here at Google Meet
are excited to announce

00:07:22.934 --> 00:07:27.100
a brand-new feature to make your
experience better than ever.

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.300
That's right --
when you click "New Meeting,"

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.033
it will take you
directly to Zoom.

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.334
Google Meet --
at least we're not Skype.

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:37.300
-Yeah, isn't that amazing?
That's amazing.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.934
[ Applause ]

00:07:38.934 --> 00:07:42.000
[ Laughs ]

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.200
And, finally, a pair of
107-year-old sisters in Japan

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.701
just claimed the title of
world's oldest identical twins.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.200
Yeah, and just to
creep people out,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.300
they stand in the hallway of
their retirement home and say,

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.734
"Come play with us."

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:58.701
Today is officially
the first day of fall.

00:07:58.701 --> 00:08:01.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:04.000
Of course, some people are
sad that summer's over,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.200
but good news -- thanks
to climate change, it's not.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.601
That's right -- we're entering
that magical time of year where

00:08:11.601 --> 00:08:14.701
we put on old jackets hoping
to find cash in the pockets.

00:08:14.701 --> 00:08:17.200
You know? Some gum!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.801
Let's get to some news.

00:08:18.801 --> 00:08:20.434
After speaking here
in New York City

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:23.100
at the UN General Assembly,
President Biden

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.234
is back in Washington, and
today, he hosted world leaders

00:08:26.234 --> 00:08:29.300
for a virtual summit
about COVID.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.200
Yep, world leaders
traveled 4,000 miles to New York

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.834
just so they could Zoom from
their rooms at the Best Western.

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:42.400
Well, the summit lasted
more than four hours.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.267
Four hours! By the end,
everyone was fatigued.

00:08:45.267 --> 00:08:47.067
Everyone had body aches,
sore throats.

00:08:47.067 --> 00:08:50.100
They were like, "Wait.
Do we have COVID?"

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.067
But the big takeaway from
the summit is that Biden

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:54.734
wants world leaders
to fully vaccinate 70%

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.234
of their population.

00:08:56.234 --> 00:09:00.067
Then world leaders were like,
"Okay, you first."

00:09:00.067 --> 00:09:02.667
[ Applause ]

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:04.834
"Deal. You..."

00:09:06.534 --> 00:09:08.801
But this is good -- at the
summit, Biden announced that

00:09:08.801 --> 00:09:11.834
the U.S. is buying an additional
500 million doses of

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:14.834
the Pfizer vaccine to share with
countries around the world.

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:17.567
Each country
will receive a basket with

00:09:17.567 --> 00:09:19.667
an injectable arrangement,
which is interesting.

00:09:19.667 --> 00:09:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.234
That's right --
The White House says

00:09:24.234 --> 00:09:27.567
they're gonna start
sending the doses in January.

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:29.467
Seriously? January?

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:31.834
Countries are like, "If I sign
up for Government Prime,

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:33.734
can I get that tomorrow?

00:09:33.734 --> 00:09:35.267
January? Wow."

00:09:35.267 --> 00:09:36.434
This is amazing.

00:09:36.434 --> 00:09:37.968
Last night,
the winning ticket for

00:09:37.968 --> 00:09:41.534
the $432-million
Mega Millions jackpot

00:09:41.534 --> 00:09:45.100
was sold a block away from
our studio, at Pronto Pizza.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.234
-Ooh!

00:09:47.234 --> 00:09:49.534
-When asked what they'll do with
$432 million, the winner said,

00:09:49.534 --> 00:09:50.934
"Hey, it's New York City.

00:09:50.934 --> 00:09:52.934
I'm gonna move from my studio
to a one-bedroom.

00:09:52.934 --> 00:09:56.667
Come on. Yeah."

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:59.267
Pronto Pizza!

00:09:59.267 --> 00:10:01.334
And, finally, I saw
that Aston Martin is selling

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:06.734
a James Bond car for kids,
and it costs $123,000.

00:10:06.734 --> 00:10:08.734
The kid who gets one
is going to be like,

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:12.334
"I'm a brat. Spoiled brat."

00:10:12.334 --> 00:10:14.501
Today, President Biden hosted
a White House summit

00:10:14.501 --> 00:10:17.901
with the leaders
of India, Australia, and Japan.

00:10:17.901 --> 00:10:19.968
They talked about the world's
most pressing issues,

00:10:19.968 --> 00:10:22.100
like the pandemic,
cybersecurity,

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.234
and Chris Pratt
being cast as Mario.

00:10:24.234 --> 00:10:25.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:27.734
The leaders also discussed
climate change

00:10:27.734 --> 00:10:30.200
and "supply chain" issues.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.367
Which means, in one meeting,

00:10:31.367 --> 00:10:32.968
they covered
the future of the Earth

00:10:32.968 --> 00:10:34.534
and Costco's
toilet-paper shortage.

00:10:34.534 --> 00:10:36.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.467 --> 00:10:37.968
But the meeting
hit a rough patch

00:10:37.968 --> 00:10:40.501
when the Australian
Prime Minister told Biden,

00:10:40.501 --> 00:10:42.634
"Do you know that, where
I'm from, your presidency

00:10:42.634 --> 00:10:44.567
is going down the drain
in the opposite direction?"

00:10:44.567 --> 00:10:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:48.868
Australia, India, and Japan.

00:10:48.868 --> 00:10:50.400
Meanwhile,
the French Prime Minister

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.100
was across the street like...
[ Imitates puffing cigarette ]

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.234
"Those --"
[ Laughter ]

00:10:54.234 --> 00:10:57.868
"Those betches."
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.601 --> 00:11:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:11:02.868 --> 00:11:06.434
Some more news --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:06.434 --> 00:11:07.801
[ Imitates puffing cigarette ]

00:11:07.801 --> 00:11:10.033
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:11:10.033 --> 00:11:12.501
"Those...

00:11:12.501 --> 00:11:15.868
betches."

00:11:15.868 --> 00:11:18.767
More news from Washington --
Republican Senator

00:11:18.767 --> 00:11:21.400
Chuck Grassley,
who is 88 years old,

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:25.968
announced that he's running for
another six-year term in 2022.

00:11:25.968 --> 00:11:27.501
Later, when he saw
the news coverage, he said,

00:11:27.501 --> 00:11:30.000
"Wow. Good for Chuck Grassley."

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.834 --> 00:11:35.133
When a reporter asked if he's
too old, he said "Oh, please.

00:11:35.133 --> 00:11:37.100
You sound like my great-great-
great-great-great-grandson."

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:38.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.801 --> 00:11:40.601
88? At that age,
you don't run for Senate,

00:11:40.601 --> 00:11:42.033
you run for president.

00:11:42.033 --> 00:11:44.167
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.167
-Preach!
-[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.167 --> 00:11:53.267
-"Good for Chuck Grassley."
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:53.267 --> 00:11:55.334
"I'm Chuck Grassley."
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:55.334 --> 00:11:57.234
This is fun.
I saw that Prince Harry

00:11:57.234 --> 00:11:59.300
and Meghan Markle
are here in New York,

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.834
and they started off --
[ Cheers ]

00:12:00.834 --> 00:12:02.634
They started off their trip
by meeting with

00:12:02.634 --> 00:12:05.534
Governor Kathy Hochul.
At the meeting, Prince Harry

00:12:05.534 --> 00:12:08.033
told the New York governor,
"I won't ask about your Andrew

00:12:08.033 --> 00:12:11.133
if you don't ask about mine."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.133 --> 00:12:13.934
Some COVID news.
The MTA said that they will

00:12:13.934 --> 00:12:18.901
start issuing $50 fines
to riders not wearing masks.

00:12:18.901 --> 00:12:21.067
Yep, it's $50
for not wearing a mask

00:12:21.067 --> 00:12:23.734
and $100 for not muting your
phone's keyboard when you type.

00:12:23.734 --> 00:12:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:25.467 --> 00:12:29.300
-[ Imitating keys clacking ]

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:32.300
Pbbbbb. Pbht!

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.968
[ Laughter ]

00:12:35.968 --> 00:12:39.100
"Those..."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.434
"...betches."

00:12:40.434 --> 00:12:42.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:47.334 --> 00:12:49.033
Never heard of that.
That's unbelievable.

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:50.868
Well, as I mentioned,
Nintendo just announced

00:12:50.868 --> 00:12:52.834
that in the upcoming
"Super Mario Bros." movie,

00:12:52.834 --> 00:12:55.801
Chris Pratt
will do the voice of Mario.

00:12:55.801 --> 00:12:57.934
Yep. After the news came out,
some people said Mario

00:12:57.934 --> 00:12:59.567
should be played
by an Italian actor.

00:12:59.567 --> 00:13:00.834
To which Italians said,

00:13:00.834 --> 00:13:02.534
"You know Mario
isn't a real person, right?"

00:13:02.534 --> 00:13:04.968
[ Laughter ]
Yep, Chris Pratt voicing Mario

00:13:04.968 --> 00:13:07.334
is an interesting choice,
but it turns out

00:13:07.334 --> 00:13:09.300
they considered
a lot of other people first,

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.300
and we actually got our hands
on the audition reel.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.434
-Really?
-Yeah, take a look at this.

00:13:13.434 --> 00:13:15.701
-It's a-me, Mario.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.701 --> 00:13:18.434
And nothing's more important
to me than family.

00:13:18.434 --> 00:13:21.667
Luigi is my family.
So is Toad.

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:23.868
Just 'cause Toad
doesn't look like me

00:13:23.868 --> 00:13:26.033
doesn't mean we're not family.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:26.033 --> 00:13:28.234
-What's up? I'm Mario.
[ Laughs ]

00:13:28.234 --> 00:13:31.000
Oh, my bad.
I mean, my name is Mario.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.868
Wait, wait.
That's not right, either.

00:13:32.868 --> 00:13:35.367
I meant to say,
"It's a-me, Mario."

00:13:35.367 --> 00:13:38.734
[ Laughing ]
That was awesome!

00:13:38.734 --> 00:13:42.400
-It's a-me, Mario.
And I'm a-looking for you.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.801
I'm will a-find a-you,
and I will a-kill a-you.

00:13:44.801 --> 00:13:45.834
[ Laughter ]

00:13:45.834 --> 00:13:48.934
-Oh, yeah, it's me Mario.
[ Mumbling ]

00:13:48.934 --> 00:13:53.634
Goomba and zoomba, roomba,
boom-boom to the koopa troopa.

00:13:53.634 --> 00:13:57.701
-Oh, yeah, mamma mia.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:57.701 --> 00:14:02.968
♪ I'm goin' to Nebraska,
and I'm drivin' a Jeep ♪

00:14:02.968 --> 00:14:04.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:04.501 --> 00:14:06.467
-They didn't get it.
-They didn't get it?

00:14:06.467 --> 00:14:10.801
-They didn't get the part.
-Aww.

00:14:10.801 --> 00:14:13.567
-Some more entertainment news.
I read that "Tiger King 2"

00:14:13.567 --> 00:14:16.501
is coming to Netflix
later this year.

00:14:16.501 --> 00:14:18.601
Come on. More "Tiger King"?

00:14:18.601 --> 00:14:21.133
I don't know whether to call it
a sequel or a variant.

00:14:21.133 --> 00:14:23.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.868
Some business news --
Uber Eats just introduced

00:14:29.868 --> 00:14:32.400
a new feature that lets
customers use emojis

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:35.567
to search for the food
they want.

00:14:35.567 --> 00:14:37.133
It's the only time
you can text an eggplant

00:14:37.133 --> 00:14:38.467
and actually wind up
with an eggplant.

00:14:38.467 --> 00:14:40.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:40.968 --> 00:14:43.501
-Oh!

00:14:43.501 --> 00:14:45.934
♪♪

00:14:45.934 --> 00:14:48.534
Eggplant.

00:14:48.534 --> 00:14:51.133
-[ Imitates cigarette puffing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:14:51.133 --> 00:14:53.000
-"Those betches."
[ Laughter ]

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.167
That's right.
You don't have to call,

00:14:55.167 --> 00:14:56.434
you don't have to pick it up,

00:14:56.434 --> 00:14:57.901
and now you don't even
have to type actual words.

00:14:57.901 --> 00:14:59.467
Pretty soon, they're just
gonna show up at your house

00:14:59.467 --> 00:15:01.200
and baby-bird the food
into your mouth.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.734
[ Laughter ]
[ Spits ]

00:15:04.734 --> 00:15:07.400
Finally, on Sunday night,
the Green Bay Packers

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.901
face off against
the San Francisco 49ers.

00:15:09.901 --> 00:15:11.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
Now, as you know,

00:15:11.601 --> 00:15:13.567
at the end of every season,
they give out awards

00:15:13.567 --> 00:15:15.067
like Most Valuable Player,

00:15:15.067 --> 00:15:16.767
but they also give out awards
at the beginning of the season.

00:15:16.767 --> 00:15:17.934
I'll show you what I mean.

00:15:17.934 --> 00:15:19.701
It's time for
"Tonight Show Superlatives."

00:15:19.701 --> 00:15:21.400
Here we go.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:26.834
-♪ Tonight Show Superlatives ♪

00:15:26.834 --> 00:15:28.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:28.501 --> 00:15:32.300
-Our first player is from
the 49ers, Jake Brendel.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.868
He was voted Most Likely to be

00:15:33.868 --> 00:15:35.734
Prince Harry's Cousin
Who Works at AutoZone.

00:15:35.734 --> 00:15:39.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:39.601 --> 00:15:42.734
Next up, from the Packers,
is Robert Tonyan.

00:15:42.734 --> 00:15:44.634
He was voted
Most Likely to say the Word

00:15:44.634 --> 00:15:45.901
"Sick" in His Wedding Vows.

00:15:45.901 --> 00:15:49.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:49.968 --> 00:15:52.567
"You look sick."
[ Laughter ]

00:15:52.567 --> 00:15:55.334
Next up, from the Packers,
is quarterback Aaron Rodgers.

00:15:55.334 --> 00:15:58.234
He was voted Most Likely to be
a Cool Youth Pastor who says,

00:15:58.234 --> 00:15:59.701
"You know who
the real rock star is?"

00:15:59.701 --> 00:16:06.534
and Then Point Up.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:06.534 --> 00:16:08.734
Next up,
from the Packers, is Dean Lowry.

00:16:08.734 --> 00:16:11.501
He was voted Most Likely to say,
"Oh, this is my favorite movie,"

00:16:11.501 --> 00:16:13.434
When Someone Points
a Laser Pointer at the Wall.

00:16:13.434 --> 00:16:17.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:17.601 --> 00:16:19.701
"My favorite character is dot."

00:16:19.701 --> 00:16:22.267
[ Light laughter ]

00:16:22.267 --> 00:16:25.801
Next, from the 49ers,
is Mitch Wishnowsky.

00:16:25.801 --> 00:16:28.200
He was voted Most Likely
to Have Appeared in Every Season

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.834
of "The Bachelorette"
Without Anyone Noticing.

00:16:29.834 --> 00:16:32.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:32.667 --> 00:16:35.267
"I think I know that guy."

00:16:35.267 --> 00:16:39.067
Next up, from the Packers,
is Billy Turner.

00:16:39.067 --> 00:16:42.300
He was voted Most Likely to get
Whiplash from a Low Doorframe.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:47.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:47.901 --> 00:16:50.567
Next up, from the Packers,
is Isaiah McDuffie.

00:16:50.567 --> 00:16:53.133
He was voted Most Likely
to be Drake's Wario.

00:16:53.133 --> 00:16:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:16:56.634 --> 00:16:59.234
Next up, from the Packers,
is Mason Crosby.

00:16:59.234 --> 00:17:01.334
He was voted Most Likely
to Play a Single Dad

00:17:01.334 --> 00:17:04.400
in a Hallmark Christmas Movie
Called "Alone for the Holidays."

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:17:06.067 --> 00:17:09.634
"Table for one."

00:17:09.634 --> 00:17:12.200
And, finally, from the 49ers,
we have George Kittle.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.601
He was voted Most Likely
to Throw his Bong Water

00:17:14.601 --> 00:17:16.801
Over the Coach After He Wins.

